    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Snapshots & Backups",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "EGdsQqhVk"
      },
      "description": "sum by (volume) (longhorn_snapshot_actual_size_bytes) — retained snapshots are what makes the nightly trim reclaim nothing even though old data is logically gone. This metric carries no pvc label, so the legend is the volume's PV UUID.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "id": 11,
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "EGdsQqhVk"
          },
          "expr": "topk(8, sum by (volume) (longhorn_snapshot_actual_size_bytes))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{volume}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Top volumes by retained snapshot size",
      "type": "bargauge"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "EGdsQqhVk"
      },
      "description": "sum(longhorn_backup_uploaded_data_size_bytes) — the delta each retained backup object transferred to the target, summed across every backup Longhorn still has a record of. Steps as daily-backup runs and retention rotates old backups out; it is not a running cumulative total.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 26
      },
      "id": 12,
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "EGdsQqhVk"
          },
          "expr": "sum(longhorn_backup_uploaded_data_size_bytes)",
          "legendFormat": "uploaded (retained backups)",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Backup uploaded bytes (retained set)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "EGdsQqhVk"
      },
      "description": "count(longhorn_volume_last_backup_at > 0) of 43 tracked volumes. The B2 backup target is currently disarmed, so the other volumes reading 0 is a deliberate condition, not a failure — this panel is scoped to volumes that have ever completed a backup rather than showing a raw 29-zero 'stale backup' alarm.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "fixedColor": "blue",
            "mode": "fixed"
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "id": 13,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "EGdsQqhVk"
          },
          "expr": "count(longhorn_volume_last_backup_at > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "volumes ever backed up",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Volumes with a backup on record",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 40
      },
      "id": 14,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "B2 (off-site) — storage runway",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "bf4q19tuivta8e"
      },
      "description": "B2 stored bytes against the free-tier cap, parsed from monitor-bridge's own b2_storage line. B2 exposes no usage API, so this log line is the only record — there is no metric to fall back on. The check pages at the cap; this panel is the runway ahead of it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "unit": "decgbytes"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/cap/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ],
                  "fill": "dash"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41
      },
      "id": 15,
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "bf4q19tuivta8e"
          },
          "expr": "avg(avg_over_time({container=\"monitor-bridge\"} |= \"B2 storage\" | regexp `B2 storage (?P<used_gb>[0-9.]+) GB of (?P<cap_gb>[0-9.]+) GB \\((?P<pct>[0-9]+)%\\), (?P<versions>[0-9]+) versions` | unwrap used_gb [$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "stored",
          "queryType": "range",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "bf4q19tuivta8e"
          },
          "expr": "avg(avg_over_time({container=\"monitor-bridge\"} |= \"B2 storage\" | regexp `B2 storage (?P<used_gb>[0-9.]+) GB of (?P<cap_gb>[0-9.]+) GB \\((?P<pct>[0-9]+)%\\), (?P<versions>[0-9]+) versions` | unwrap cap_gb [$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "cap",
          "queryType": "range",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "B2 stored vs free-tier cap",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "bf4q19tuivta8e"
      },
      "description": "Percent of the B2 free-tier storage cap in use. b2_storage pages above its own ceiling; this is the headroom read at a glance.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
